# 基本図形編集をプロセスで開き、その中の仮身から開いたウインドウが、閉じるときに元の仮身へ
# 書き戻すこと(DT_RQ_OPEN の DT_F_LINK、design 11.3), for tools/ui_run.py. figproc 1
# makes every figure open with the process. Two copies of 画用紙 (A of 30 rectangles, B of
# 2000, wider than the window) and a text (mkbig doc) are linked into BTRON, the desktop's
# first window. A is opened from its link (the process P); the links of B and of the text are
# copied to the tray in BTRON and pasted into A. B opened from its link in A is another
# process, given that link of A's record: scrolled and closed, its view goes to P, which
# writes it into its record; 新たな実身に保存 in B puts a link to the copy into A, by P. The
# text opened from its link in A is a window of the desktop's: scrolled and closed, its view
# goes to P the same way. A closed and opened again holds the three links; a shape of
# it carried out over BTRON stays where it was, and one let go on the ground moves there.
# Keys with Ctrl (01): C 06, V 19, E 08; Enter 28.
mkbig fig 30 4
figproc 1
linkbig 180 45
mkbig fig 2000 2
linkbig 180 95
mkbig doc 80
linkbig 190 70
wait 300
click 230 104
wait 300
key 06 01
wait 300
logmark
dclick 190 52
expectsincein 60 figure: opened 画用紙 shapes 32 links 0 autoref 1 parent 1
wait 800
click 600 500
wait 300
logmark
key 19 01
expectsince figure: pasted, 33 shapes 1 picked
click 600 500
wait 300
# B, from its link in A: a process given the link of A's record
logmark
dclick 340 221
expectsincein 60 figure: opened 画用紙 shapes 2002 links 0 autoref 1 parent 1
wait 1500
shot pl_b
# B is wider than the window: scrolled across by its bar
drag 480 690 700 690
wait 1000
shot pl_b_scrolled
# 新たな実身に保存 in B: the copy's link goes into A, by P
logmark
click 500 400 1
wait 500
move 510 440
wait 300
move 650 440
move 650 461
wait 300
click 650 461
expectsince figure: chosen save.new
wait 800
key 28
expectsince figure: saved as new (0)
expectsince figure: a link to the copy saved put with its link
wait 500
logmark
key 08 01
expectsince figure: link view written back:
absent link view written back: 0,0 zoom 100
wait 800
shot pl_b_closed
# the text, from its link in A: a window of the desktop's. A's 道具パネル (100,0 to 498,112)
# stands over BTRON's links, as the desktop's own figure editor's does: BTRON is brought
# forward by its band first, and the panel, subordinate to A, goes out of sight meanwhile
click 50 14
wait 300
click 250 79
wait 300
key 06 01
wait 300
click 600 500
wait 300
logmark
key 19 01
expectsince figure: pasted, 35 shapes 1 picked
wait 500
click 600 500
wait 300
logmark
dclick 400 211
wait 1500
shot pl_doc
wheel -5
wait 1000
shot pl_doc_scrolled
key 08 01
expectsince figure: link view written back: 0,
wait 500
# A closed and opened again: the links of B, of its copy and of the text are there
logmark
click 600 500
wait 300
key 08 01
expectsince figure: saved (0)
expectsince figure: closed
wait 800
logmark
dclick 190 52
expectsincein 60 figure: opened 画用紙 shapes 35 links 3 autoref 1 parent 1
wait 800
shot pl_a_again
# a shape alone carried out and let go over BTRON, a window of the desktop's that links are
# carried into: only links leave a figure's window, so it stays where it was (DT_RQ_LET_GO),
# and BTRON takes the keys
logmark
move 260 163
down
move 240 170
wait 500
move 90 190
wait 500
move 50 190
wait 1000
up
expectsince figure: let go over another window: nothing moved
absent figure: moved 1 by
wait 500
shot pl_let_go
# let go on the ground, where no window is: it moves, as in the desktop's own figure editor
click 600 500
wait 300
logmark
move 260 163
down
move 240 300
wait 500
move 240 750
wait 500
up
expectsince figure: moved 1 by -20,587
wait 500
click 600 500
wait 300
key 08 01
expectsince figure: closed
absent !OACV!
